{
  "_comment": [
    "The population `denial_rate.py` measures: commands a role in this repository",
    "legitimately runs. The rate is the share of them that `command_actions.classify`",
    "grades to an action no role holds, which is the usability cost of the allowlist.",
    "",
    "This file is a protected path on purpose. The corpus is the gate's population,",
    "and a gate whose population the measured party can edit measures nothing:",
    "deleting the denied entries would drive the rate to zero without changing the",
    "classifier. Adding an entry is a reviewed change, like raising any other ratchet.",
    "",
    "`why` is the reason the command is in the corpus at all. An entry nobody can",
    "justify is not evidence of a false denial; it is a command that should deny."
  ],
  "commands": [
